{number: 79}
{title: A Mighty Fortress Is Our God}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A [D] mighty [A] fortress [D] is our [G] God,
A [D] bulwark [A7] never [D] failing;
Our Helper He, a-[A] mid the [G] flood
Of [D] mortal [A7] ills pre-[D] vailing:
For [Bm] still our [A] ancient [D] foe
Doth [G] seek to [D] work us [A] woe;
His [Bm] craft and [A] pow'r are [D] great,
And, [G] armed with [D] cruel [A] hate,
On [Bm] earth is [A] not his [D] e-[G]-[D] [A7]-[D] qual.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Did [D] we in [A] our own [D] strength con-[G] fide,
Our [D] striving [A7] would be [D] losing;
Were not the right Man [A] on our [G] side,
The [D] Man of [A7] God's own [D] choosing:
Dost [Bm] ask who [A] that may [D] be?
Christ [G] Jesus, [D] it is [A] He;
Lord [Bm] Saba-[A] oth, His [D] Name,
From [G] age to [D] age the [A] same,
And [Bm] He must [A] win the [D] bat-[G]-[D] [A7]-[D] tle.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [D] though this [A] world, with [D] devils [G] filled,
Should [D] threaten [A7] to un-[D] do us,
We will not fear, for [A] God hath [G] willed
His [D] truth to [A7] triumph [D] through us:
The [Bm] Prince of [A] Darkness [D] grim,
We [G] tremble [D] not for [A] him;
His [Bm] rage we [A] can en-[D] dure,
For [G] lo, his [D] doom is [A] sure,
One [Bm] little [A] word shall [D] fell [G]-[D] [A7]-[D] him.
{end_of_verse}
